  "instructions": [
    "Air Fryer Option: Preheat the air fryer to 180°C (350°F).",
    "Season the 400g diced chicken breast with garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Spray lightly with low-calorie cooking spray and place the chicken in the air fryer basket.",
    "Cook for 10-12 minutes, shaking halfway through, until fully cooked and golden brown.",
    "Pan Option: Heat a non-stick pan over medium heat and spray lightly with low-calorie cooking spray. Add the seasoned chicken and cook for 6-8 minutes until the chicken is fully cooked and browned.",
    "After the chicken has cooked, transfer it to a bowl and toss it with the honey and BBQ sauce, ensuring the chicken is evenly coated.",
    "Let the chicken cook for an additional 1-2 minutes to caramelize the sauce slightly.",
    "Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil, and cook the pasta according to the package instructions.",
    "Before draining, reserve about 1/4 cup of pasta water to help with the cheese sauce later. Drain the pasta and set aside.",
    "In a blender, combine the cottage cheese, light cream cheese, grated cheese, milk, garlic powder, parsley, black pepper, paprika, salt, and mustard. Blend until smooth and creamy.",
    "Pour the cheese sauce into a saucepan and heat over medium-low heat, stirring occasionally.",
    "If the sauce becomes too thick, add a splash of the reserved pasta water to loosen it and make it extra creamy.",
    "Cook for 3-5 minutes until the sauce thickens and becomes smooth.",
    "Once the cheese sauce is ready, add the cooked pasta to the sauce, stirring to coat the pasta evenly.",
    "Add more pasta water if needed to reach your desired consistency.",
    "Let the mac and cheese sit for 10 minutes to allow the flavours to meld and the sauce to thicken.",
    "Serve the cheesy pasta in bowls and top each portion with the Honey BBQ Chicken.",
    "Garnish with a sprinkle of parsley for a fresh touch."
  ],
